MW4 V3.1 verified-anchor proposal architecture qualification

Single executable semantic path:
evidence analysis -> direct-interaction hostile verification -> hard-gap-safe verified support components -> boundary-refined canonical clip proposals -> integrity/quality gates -> canonical adaptive allocator -> FFV1/NUT renderer.

The base V3.1 module remains evidence-only. The obsolete refined planner, historical semantic planner, detached Finishing Move body planner, fallback guard, legacy allocation contract, allocator patch layer, and allocation regression shim remain physically absent from the executable path.

Combat-island evidence is no longer treated as the final editorial boundary. Verified hostile events seed maximal same-shot hard-gap-free support components; clip proposals are then refined only inside those support regions. Normal plans may use multiple source-native 1.0x same-shot proposal segments when rejected hard-gap material is omitted explicitly. No proposal segment may cross a hard combat gap, source shot, verified source cut, excluded window, or protected Finishing Move hero region.

Batch2 Finishing Move policy remains strict: protected verified hero at 1.0x, then only boundary-refined moments contained inside verified hostile/payoff support components. Every body moment still requires independently verified hostile payoff plus the unchanged component retention/payoff/weakest-quarter/inactivity floors; the terminal moment must also pass the unchanged ending-quality floor. The hero-aware >=10 second final-duration contract, <=15.5 second Finishing Move maximum, maximum body-moment duration, first-continuation reach, hard-cut source-gap contract, and adaptive allocator requirement are unchanged.

Every hostile event still requires local direct-interaction confirmation. Contact, motion, HUD/color/minimap state and ambiguous actors remain non-hostile. The centered MW4 hitmarker geometry remains pinned at outer-radius fraction 0.105 and the acceptance threshold remains 0.34. No hostile, editorial, duration or quality threshold is lowered.

Canonical hard-gap checks retain half-open frame-grid semantics with bounded millisecond-rounding tolerance. Regression tests continue to cover rounded-up terminal bounds, rounded-down opening bounds, true hard-gap rejection, orphaned verified-hostile recovery, and structural non-islandable evidence disposition.

The proposal layer emits explicit diagnostics for support-component count, candidate chains, proposal combinations, duration rejection, integrity rejection, quality rejection, qualified plans, required Finishing Move body duration, maximum qualified body seconds seen, and threshold_reduction_used=false.

Fail-closed allocation remains mandatory. If verified evidence cannot satisfy the campaign contract, allocation exits non-zero and surfaces structured diagnostics rather than manufacturing a clip, re-enabling semantic montage, or lowering gates.

Existing source certification, exact decoded-frame hash identity, FFV1 level-3 + PCM s16le NUT staging/stitched/canonical transport, source-native delivery timing/metadata restoration, SSIM >= 0.99, PSNR >= 40 dB and no crop/scale/zoom qualification contracts remain mandatory.

